        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Len Reynolds, H. V. Evatt, Sir Edmund Barton\n- Organizations: Australian Labor Party\n- Places: Division of Barton, New South Wales, Australia\n- Concepts: Australian electoral divisions\n\nFacts:\n- The Division of Barton was created in 1922 in New South Wales, Australia.\n- The Division of Barton is named for Sir Edmund Barton, the first Prime Minister of Australia.\n- The Division of Barton is an Australian electoral division in the state of New South Wales.\n- In 1958, Len Reynolds was selected as the Australian Labor Party candidate for the seat of Barton.\n- In 1958, H. V. Evatt was leaving the seat of Barton because it was perceived to be too marginal.",
